  "id": "COMPOUND:18030 - PROTEIN:5781",
  "verbalization": "Ustusol A appears to have a potential relationship with A2780cisR through multiple indirect pathways, with the core mechanism involving the inhibition of a target protein that ultimately affects A2780cisR. The evidence suggests that Ustusol A acts as a target for MOVP-3, which is inhibited by Neridienone A, and that Neridienone A, in turn, targets A2780cisR. Similarly, Ustusol A may also target HuT78, which is inhibited by Methylseleno carboxyethylglutamine, which also targets A2780cisR. These pathways highlight a shared mechanism of action involving the inhibition of a target protein that ultimately leads to the modulation of A2780cisR. The integration of these pathways suggests that Ustusol A may exert its effects through a mechanism that involves the inhibition of a target protein, which is then further modulated by other compounds, ultimately influencing A2780cisR. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between Ustusol A and A2780cisR, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
